{
    "_notes": "Bosch BME680 (temperature, pressure, humidity, gas) at 0x76 (SDO low) or 0x77 (SDO high, Adafruit default). Detection: chip ID (0xD0) 0x61 and variant (0xF0) 0x00 - a BME688 (variant 0x01) has another data layout. Forced mode only, so each poll triggers a measurement (ctrl_meas 0x74 = 0x25: temperature and pressure x1, forced), waits 200 ms (TPH plus the 152 ms heater time) and reads the calibration (0x89 25 bytes, 0xE1 16 bytes, 0x00 5 bytes) and the data (0x1D 15 bytes); the decode code applies Bosch's floating-point compensation and gas-resistance calculation (range lookup tables as if-chains); gas is 0 unless gas valid and heater stable are both set. Init: soft reset, 10 ms; ctrl_hum 0x01; config 0x00 (filter off); gas_wait_0 0x66 (152 ms); res_heat_0 0x6E; ctrl_gas_1 0x10 (run gas, heater profile 0). res_heat_0 is FIXED: the right value is calculated per unit from its calibration (par_g1-g3, res_heat_range, res_heat_val) and the ambient temperature, which a fixed init string can't do; 0x6E is the value for one unit at 320 C (0x6D-0x6E over 15-35 C ambient), so on other units the hot plate temperature differs by some tens of degrees and gas resistance is a relative trend, not comparable between units. See devdocs/computed-init-values.md for the proposed fix. 0x76 is also a common multiplexer address (Axiom018's).",
